Patch: 007-code-mode-nested
Reason: a host tool a code-mode model's script calls arrives as a nested call under an id of Codex's own (exec-<uuid>) that no rollout line carries, so a never tool's barrier waited for a line that never comes and the call was declined for good; it is durable once the exec it runs under is in the log, and it is tied to that exec
Upstream: ours
Pins: code mode: an exec that calls a never host tool runs it exactly once
Pins: code mode: two nested calls of one exec (a Promise.all) each pass the barrier once, under the one exec, and run once
